                <!-- object Csi2Rfe20Usage  -->
                <bool id="Csi2Rfe20Usage" label="RFE 2.0 Abstract Usage" available="($configSet.Is_S32R41.getValue())">
                    <description>
                        <![CDATA[<html> This parameter specify if for S32R41 platform the RFE 2.0 Abstract is used.
                        If this is used, the CSI2 interface needs a very specific setup, to align the needs of RFE Abstract 2.0 for Front-End (TEF82XX, etc.) BIST :
                        <b>- Virtual Channel 3 reserved for BIST data reception
                        - the correct setup for data to be received
                        - usage of a very specific physical address for data to be received, aligned to the one specified in the RFE Abstract 2.0 Tresos plugin</b>
                        As it will be detected after files generation, this feature is connected to and needs the files generated from RFE Abstract 2.0 plugin.
                        All necesssary Virtual Channel 3 definitions will be added to the Csi2_PBCfg.c file, but using the same <b>RFE_RFBIST_BUFFERS_ADDRESS</b> address.
                        As each Front-End needs the own BIST buffer and the BIST buffer memory allocation is contiguous, at file generation time the buffers will be aligned to
                        modulo <b>RFE_NUM_USED_FRONT_ENDS</b> basis, the BIST buffer start for the n-th CSI2 setup starting at <b>RFE_RFBIST_BUFFERS_ADDRESS + (1024 * (n % RFE_NUM_USED_FRONT_ENDS))</b>
                        If the CSI2 units setup is registered in the normal order, the resulted configuration will be perfect. If not, it will be necessary to adjust manually the BIST buffer start in the resulted Csi2_PBCfg.c file.
                        <b>TRUE</b>: RFE 2.0 Abstract to be used.</P>
                        <b>FALSE</b>: RFE 2.0 Abstract not used.</html>]]>
                    </description>
                    <options_expr>
                        <option id="type" expr="`BOOLEAN`"/>
                        <option id="UUID" expr="`ECUC:2beea917-2bcd-497c-a2ed-c8285559c370`"/>
                        <option id="postBuildVariantValue" expr="false"/>
                        <option id="SYNC_VALUE"/>
                        <option id="origin" expr="`NXP`"/>
                        <option id="symbolicNameValue" expr="false"/>
                        <option id="defaultValue" expr="`false`"/>
                        <option id="scope" expr="`LOCAL`"/>
